NETBBPROBE(1)

NAME
    netbbprobe - test BusyBox-facing network compatibility paths

SYNOPSIS
    netbbprobe

DESCRIPTION
    netbbprobe is a guest regression probe for the classic BusyBox networking
    surface. It checks eth0 and loopback interface discovery, ifconfig-style
    ioctls, minimal rtnetlink link/address/route/neighbor dumps, runtime IPv4
    address and netmask updates, default-route add/delete, /proc/net/dev,
    /proc/net/route, UDP datagram basics, localhost and numeric IPv4 resolver
    paths, and error behavior for network ioctls on non-socket descriptors.

    The probe is installed under /usr/libexec/tests and is normally run by the
    host-driven selftest suite rather than by hand.

SEE ALSO
    busybox(1), compatprobe(1), selftest(1), smallos(7)
